# Project structure standard

Every Python data/extract/reporting project in this workspace should follow the same shape:

## Required root files

- `config.yaml` — **all** runtime configuration (paths, API, retries, feature flags). Secrets use `${ENV_VAR}` only.
- `run.py` — single CLI entrypoint (`python run.py ...`).
- `config.py` — thin loader that reads `config.yaml` and expands `${ENV_VAR}`; no hardcoded business settings.
- `requirements.txt`
- `README.md`
- `.env.example` (never commit real `.env`)

## Do

- Put new tunables in `config.yaml`, then expose them via `config.py`.
- Keep implementation under `src/` (or `extract/`) and templates under `report/` / `templates/`.
- Document commands and proxy/env setup in `README.md`.

## Do not

- Hardcode timeouts, URLs, paths, or feature flags in Python modules.
- Commit secrets, proxies with credentials, or `.env`.
- Invent alternate entrypoints without keeping `run.py` at the repo root.

## Related skill

When migrating legacy code into this layout, use the `extract-configs-to-yaml` skill before editing `config.yaml`.
